description:
## Problem

`packages/swf/src/sprite.ts` does not apply the `registrationPoint` offset when placing SymbolInstance objects inside a sprite (symbol) timeline, but `compile.ts` does (lines 1716–1723):

```ts
// compile.ts lines 1716-1723 (CORRECT):
if (displayObj.type === "instance" && displayObj.registrationPoint) {
  x -= displayObj.registrationPoint.x;
  y -= displayObj.registrationPoint.y;
}
```

`sprite.ts` has no equivalent code — it reads `x` and `y` directly from the display object without subtracting the registration point offset.

## Impact

Any SymbolInstance placed inside another symbol's timeline that has a non-zero `registrationPoint` will be placed at the wrong position. This is a silent SWF encoding error — the instance appears offset from its correct position in Ruffle. Affects nested symbols where the inner instance has a non-origin registration point (common for rotatable/scalable symbols).

## Fix

In `sprite.ts`, after extracting `x`/`y` from the display object (around line 432–438), add the same registrationPoint subtraction that compile.ts applies:

```ts
// In sprite.ts, after extracting x/y/scaleX/scaleY/rotation/skewX/skewY:
if (displayObj.type === "instance") {
  const inst = displayObj as import("@flash/core").SymbolInstance;
  if (inst.registrationPoint) {
    x -= inst.registrationPoint.x;
    y -= inst.registrationPoint.y;
  }
}
```

This must be inserted in both the `isFirst` path and the `posChanged` path (the extraction happens once before the branch, so one insertion suffices). The code applies to both the first-placement and move branches since `x`/`y` are read before the `isFirst`/`posChanged` check.

## Files

- `packages/swf/src/sprite.ts` — around line 432 (inside the per-depth loop, after extracting transform)
- Reference: `packages/swf/src/compile.ts` lines 1716–1723
